      <h4>Items to review in support planning</h4><ul><li><code>P-W1</code> — Can say or explain a familiar Chinese word but has difficulty remembering its written characters. <strong>(3/5 · Sometimes)</strong></li><li><code>P-W2</code> — Expresses ideas less fully in Chinese writing than when discussing a similar topic aloud. <strong>(3/5 · Sometimes)</strong></li><li><code>P-W4</code> — Has difficulty putting familiar Chinese words or phrases together into a meaningful written sentence. <strong>(3/5 · Sometimes)</strong></li><li><code>P-W5</code> — Has difficulty arranging ideas clearly in a Chinese written response. <strong>(3/5 · Sometimes)</strong></li><li><code>P-W7</code> — Leaves out, adds, or changes the order of Chinese characters or words in ways that change the intended written meaning. <strong>(3/5 · Sometimes)</strong></li></ul>
